1395 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (This is meant to be a tool for understanding the steps for creating decision trees, Markov models, and/or microsimulation models for health economic evaluation. Simulation modeling is a technique used to represent the progression of a health condition/disease process over time by integrating biological processes/mechanisms, patient behaviors, and healthcare system factors. These models enable researchers to examine the impact of clinical decisions \(like different strategies of care\)  or policy \(like changes to insurance coverage\) on long-term outcomes \(like quality of life\). )
/E (This is meant to be a tool for understanding the steps for creating decision trees, Markov models, and/or microsimulation models for health economic evaluation. Simulation modeling is a technique used to represent the progression of a health condition/disease process over time by integrating biological processes/mechanisms, patient behaviors, and healthcare system factors. These models enable researchers to examine the impact of clinical decisions \(like different strategies of care\)  or policy \(like changes to insurance coverage\) on long-term outcomes \(like quality of life\). )
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
