2659 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T (In real life, time is continuous and therefore events can happen at any time in a cycle. However, in Markov and microsimulation models, events occur at the beginning or the end of the cycle. To remediate the overcounting or undercounting this can cause, half-cycle correction is applied to the model. There are other forms of correction but half-cycle is enough for most models. )
/E (In real life, time is continuous and therefore events can happen at any time in a cycle. However, in Markov and microsimulation models, events occur at the beginning or the end of the cycle. To remediate the overcounting or undercounting this can cause, half-cycle correction is applied to the model. There are other forms of correction but half-cycle is enough for most models. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
