<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (DALYs and QALYs are both measures of health outcomes but represent opposite concepts. QALYs measure health gains \(Healthy = 1\) and DALYs measure disease burden \(Healthy = 0\). In health economic models, QALYs are maximized, while DALYs are minimized. Both can be used for cost-effectiveness analysis, but they require different data inputs and interpretation. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [26]
